  <revision rev="8" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>08ceb9349352d520bcd8afa58d9a44b1</srcmd5>
    <version>3.5.0</version>
    <time>1785344461</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 3.5.0 and clean up the spec

Upstream 3.5.0 (first release since 3.4.3 in 2019) adds LAS 1.5 support,
renames get/set_classification_uni to get/set_classification, merges the
LASMessage concept from LAStools and fixes several leaks plus an integer
overflow in laszip_update_inventory and fseek on &gt;2GB las/lax files.

ABI: the shared library keeps soname 8 (upstream sets LASZIP_SO_VERSION
8.0.6, compatibility version 8). Comparing exported symbols against the
3.4.3 currently in Factory: 878 vs 710, with four internal
LASindex/LASinterval symbols withdrawn. Nothing in Factory build-depends on
laszip, so there is no consumer of the withdrawn symbols. Fedora carries a
patch restoring the LASzipper/LASunzipper C++ API; it is not needed here
because those symbols were never exported by our build and we never shipped
the corresponding headers.

Packaging: upstream stopped attaching a release tarball (and its detached
sha256sum) after 3.4.3, so the source moves to the git archive. Adds a
%check -- upstream has no test suite, so the deliberately corrupt LAZ files
under data/ are pushed through the public C API and each must be rejected,
which also covers the dlopen path in liblaszip_api. The whole laszip include
directory is now packaged so a new upstream header cannot break the build
again, as laszip_common.h did. Also tracks the upstream rename of COPYING,
AUTHORS and ChangeLog to .txt, normalises CRLF in README.md, replaces the
hand-written ldconfig scriptlets with %ldconfig_scriptlets and drops Group.

Built on aarch64: 0 rpmlint badness, 0 warnings, source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1368326</requestid>
  </revision>
